body:
@D-Roberts PTAL when you've got a moment 

  * currently this supports the NOVA-lite model but other ones from the NOVA family can be added TITAN family models are not supported in batch mode by aws bedrock at the moment so they cannot be tested.

I can share the credentials for aws account via other channels.

- Removed the node_modules file from git tracking on the backend directory;
- Installed key dependencies on the backend (types/express, prisma, cors, prisma/client);
- Set up initial configs on prisma, and connected to my postgreSQL database;
- Created the first model on my prisma.schema to test the connection and it worked;
- Started to work on app.ts by setting up basic configs like the port config, and the prismaClient instance creation;
